{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4528","id":4734112836,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGizURA","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4528","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4528.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4528.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4528","number":4528,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A29-T05.9: retain reproducible campaigns and ordinary corpus replay","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A29-T05.9\nRelated: #1151; depends on merged #4527\n\n## Change\n\nExpose the fixed eight-target harness through a bounded CLI and retain clean-source reports, per-target SHA-256 report links, seed/budget metadata, and literal reproduction argv arrays. Output directories and report files must be new. Missing targets, source changes, cancellation, unsupported results and incomplete replay cannot produce a passing aggregate.\n\nThe ordinary A29 test manifest now discovers reviewed hash-named corpus records. Replay preserves original bytes and limits; a continuing finding or integrity failure fails. An empty corpus is an explicit skipped qualification, not a manufactured pass.\n\nAdd a manual, read-only GitHub workflow using existing pinned actions and Node version, quoted environment inputs, serial wrappers, checkout integrity and always-retained findings. The coverage document lists actual APIs, every resource ceiling, unsupported profiles, and the source/evidence contract.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Local commit `7d7a7c000cd1f79dff7d959ac1ce368b86d44577`: CLI/report/ordinary-corpus tests **6 passed, 0 failed, 1 explicit empty-corpus skip**.\n- Published tree `fa14e70cf758103df72e15d514a7efdde5d127a8` exactly matches that locally tested tree; GitHub object publication produced a different commit ID.\n- Previous integrated CLI run at clean commit `07c833a82084b8fc07e4d9263bf83e315998e1ab`: 256 completed seed-1 cases, 37 accepted, 213 controlled rejections, 6 unsupported, zero findings; aggregate **unsupported**, exit 2. This run predates the additive reproduction metadata and is not exact-head qualification.\n- That integrated source passed static checks and production build. Hosted PR core is the publication gate; normal core does not execute the Node suite.\n\n## Remaining acceptance\n\nThe prevailing [serial validation policy](planning/qualification/serial-validation.md) explicitly disables specialty schedules. This workflow therefore remains manual: #1151's older nightly criterion is policy-deferred and the issue stays open. This PR does not change CI-wide scheduling, Project fields, credentials, release permissions or active owner reservations.\n\nNo production crash inputs have yet been promoted. Adapter follow-ups cover semantic protocol requests, actual bounded workspace import, pinned PDB corpus and fixed native-host checks. Full IL image idempotence, general verified-bytecode execution and native/other-platform qualification remain separate obligations. Ordinary green checks are not evidence for those obligations.\n\nNo dependencies or product package changes.\n","created_at":"2026-10-04T11:50:25Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T11:51:55Z","closed_at":"2026-10-04T11:51:55Z","merged_at":"2026-10-04T11:51:55Z","merge_commit_sha":"003654ce10a49889f8def8f269dff059223e5eee","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12525232279,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU59Ms88AAAAC6o_glw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/labels/size/XL","name":"size/XL","color":"C32607","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4528/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4528/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4528/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/statuses/739881471ea5a5b88c263321982cbe7b5c11b44d","head":{"label":"wieslawsoltes:codex/p4-fuzz-cli","ref":"codex/p4-fuzz-cli","sha":"739881471ea5a5b88c263321982cbe7b5c11b44d","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions"